+\section{Limitations and Conclusion}
+The study concerns one checkpoint, two package distributions, one fixed 2,048-token cap, strict format compliance, truncation risk, fixed scorers, and a finite six-family target. Independent-draw spoilage is not a causal switch; finite $K$ yields noisy input targets; and $d_\epsilon$ and expected score capture losses omitted by perfect correctness. An aggregate audit can miss family heterogeneity and cannot transfer to renderer or external-suite shift. Empirical-Bernstein validity depends on the frozen bounded ledger and independent complete clusters. Renderer cases not paired by latent ID remain unpaired descriptions. The same-rollout empirical oracle is optimistic. No non-significant contrast will be called equivalence.
+
+\TC{} asks whether paired benefit and independent-draw spoilage supervision improves a constrained choice between \D{} and \Rpol{} beyond same-resource winner and factorized outcome routers. Package freeze precedes labels; tuning selects once; each method is audited once; failure forces direct; and test superiority is adjudicated separately. The development history above is disclosed, but no learned-router comparison, audit passage, power estimate, final-test result, or novel effect is established.
+
+\subsection*{Reproducibility statement}
+The original reference plus approved CR01 and accepted operational clarifications govern this active revision; the eventual reviewed, dated, hash-linked study and child manifests will govern execution. Before test access, the release will archive immutable hashes for packages, prompts, parsers, features, data splits, candidates, audit code, cost schedule, random streams, and fallback. Historical conflicting notes remain marked superseded. Outputs will be released only where licenses permit; otherwise permitted identifiers, hashes, derived cluster rows, and evaluation code will be provided.
+
+\subsection*{AI use statement (draft stage)}
+Generative AI assisted literature organization, critique-driven protocol revision, prose editing, BibTeX preparation, and vector figure layout. AI-assisted engineering also implemented and documented the bounded local DEVELOPMENT diagnostics. No final gate training, audit, or test was performed; the CR01 adoption itself used no model compute. Authors must verify every source, protocol component, artifact, and claim before submission and retain responsibility for the final work.
